        <h1>LeetCode 3875: Construct Uniform Parity Array I (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                You are given an array nums1 of n distinct integers. Construct another array nums2 of length n such
                that all elements in nums2 are either odd or even. For each index i, choose exactly one of the
                following options, in any order: nums2[i] = nums1[i], or nums2[i] = nums1[i] - nums1[j] for an index
                j != i. Return true if it is possible to construct nums2; otherwise, return false.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example 1:</strong>
                Input: nums1 = [2,3]<br>
                Output: true<br>
                Explanation: Choose nums2 = [-1,3] by subtracting 3 from 2 and keeping 3. Both elements are odd.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example 2:</strong>
                Input: nums1 = [4,6]<br>
                Output: true<br>
                Explanation: Choose nums2 = [4,6]. Both elements are even.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Constraints:</strong>
                1 &lt;= n == nums1.length &lt;= 100, 1 &lt;= nums1[i] &lt;= 100, and nums1 consists of distinct
                integers.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    bool uniformArray(vector<int>& nums1) {
		bool hasEven = false;
		bool hasOdd = false;
        for (int value : nums1) {
			hasEven |= (value % 2 == 0);
			hasOdd |= (value % 2 != 0);
		}
		return hasEven || hasOdd;
	}
};</code></pre>
